    "message": "fix(upgrade): make the sweep-before-download order structural, not a comment\n\nThe PR notes the sweep call had to move above the download and says there is\nnow a test for it. There was not: the two new cases pin which prefixes the\nsweep reclaims, but the ordering lived inline in the command action where no\ntest could reach it. Moving the call back below the download — which breaks\nevery upgrade on every platform, since the sweep then deletes the archive it\nis about to extract — left all 724 tests passing.\n\nBoth call sites now go through `prepareDownloadDir()`, which does mkdir,\nsweep, mkdtemp in that order and is directly testable. Three cases cover it:\nan earlier run's scratch is reclaimed while the new one survives, an\ninterrupted install is restored before any download happens, and IX_HOME is\ncreated when a manual install never did. Inverting the order inside the\nhelper fails all three.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
